{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nThe user wants me to implement a `solve(case)` function for HDBSCAN mutual-reachability MST computation. Let me analyze the requirements:\n\n1. For each pair, compute mutual reachability as `max(core_left, core_right, distance)`\n2. Canonicalize undirected endpoints (sort edge endpoints)\n3. Sort by reachability then endpoint IDs\n4. Run Kruskal with deterministic union-find until n-1 edges selected\n5. Reject disconnected inputs\n6. Return selected edges plus total weight\n\nThe response must be a single JSON object with key \"implementation\" containing Python source code.\n\nLet me write the implementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    import copy\n    \n    # Validate required fields\n    if \"nodes\" not in case:\n        raise ValueError(\"Missing required field: nodes\")\n    if \"core_distance\" not in case:\n        raise ValueError(\"Missing required field: core_distance\")\n    if \"distances\" not in case:\n        raise ValueError(\"Missing required field: distances\")\n    \n    nodes = list(case[\"nodes\"])\n    core_distance = dict(case[\"core_distance\"])\n    distances = list(case[\"distances\"])\n    \n    n = len(nodes)\n    if n == 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"No nodes provided\")\n    \n    # Validate all nodes have core distances\n    for node in nodes:\n        if node not in core_distance:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Missing core distance for node: {node}\")\n    \n    # Compute mutual reachability edges\n    mr_edges = []\n    for edge in distances:\n        if len(edge) != 3:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Invalid edge format: {edge}\")\n        u, v, dist = edge[0], edge[1], edge[2]\n        \n        if u not in core_distance:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Node {u} in distances not in core_distance\")\n        if v not in core_distance:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Node {v} in distances not in core_distance\")\n        \n        mr = max(core_distance[u], core_distance[v], dist)\n        \n        # Canonicalize: sort endpoints\n        if u \u003e v:\n            u, v = v, u\n        \n        mr_edges.append((mr, u, v))\n    \n    # Sort by mutual reachability, then by endpoint IDs\n    mr_edges.sort(key=lambda e: (e[0], e[1], e[2]))\n    \n    # Kruskal's algorithm with union-find\n    parent = {node: node for node in nodes}\n    rank = {node: 0 for node in nodes}\n    \n    def find(x):\n        while parent[x] != x:\n            parent[x] = parent[parent[x]]  # path compression\n            x = parent[x]\n        return x\n    \n    def union(x, y):\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\n        if rx == ry:\n            return False\n        # Union by rank\n        if rank[rx] \u003c rank[ry]:\n            rx, ry = ry, rx\n        parent[ry] = rx\n        if rank[rx] == rank[ry]:\n            rank[rx] += 1\n        return True\n    \n    selected_edges = []\n    total_weight = 0.0\n    \n    for mr, u, v in mr_edges:\n        if union(u, v):\n            selected_edges.append({\n                \"u\": u,\n                \"v\": v,\n                \"mutual_reachability\": mr\n            })\n            total_weight += mr\n            if len(selected_edges) == n - 1:\n                break\n    \n    if len(selected_edges) != n - 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input graph is disconnected; cannot form MST\")\n    \n    return {\n        \"mst_edges\": selected_edges,\n        \"total_weight\": total_weight\n    }\n```\n\nWait, I need to be careful about the union-find being deterministic. The path compression with halving might cause non-determinism in some cases. Let me think...\n\nActually, since we're sorting edges before processing them, the union-find operations will be deterministic as long as the data structures are initialized deterministically. Using dictionaries is fine since we initialize them from the sorted `nodes` list.\n\nAlso, I should preserve the original (non-canonicalized) edge identifiers for auditing purposes. Let me re-read the requirements: \"Preserve every source identifier needed to audit the decision\". So I should keep track of the original u, v from the input.\n\nLet me also check: \"Canonicalize undirected endpoints\" - this is for the sorting/deduplication step, but we should probably return the canonical form or the original form?\n\nThe requirement says \"Preserve every source identifier needed to audit the decision\". I'll return the canonical form (sorted endpoints) since those are the identifiers being used.\n\nLet me also make sure I handle the case where the same pair appears multiple times in distances (though the fixtures don't seem to have this issue).\n\nActually, re-reading: \"Sort by reachability then endpoint IDs\" - after canonicalization, sort. This is what I'm doing.\n\nLet me also think about whether I need to handle the mutation of parent/rank. Since I'm using `parent` and `rank` as local dicts, this is fine.\n\nOne issue: in the union-find with union by rank, when ranks are equal and we always put rx as the root, the choice of which root to keep could be non-deterministic if find() returns different things. Let me ensure determinism by using a tiebreak on node ID:\n\n```python\ndef union(x, y):\n    rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\n    if rx == ry:\n        return False\n    # Deterministic union by rank, then by node id for tie-breaking\n    if rank[rx] \u003c rank[ry]:\n        rx, ry = ry, rx\n    elif rank[rx] == rank[ry] and rx \u003e ry:\n        rx, ry = ry, rx\n    parent[ry] = rx\n    if rank[rx] == rank[ry]:\n        rank[rx] += 1\n    return True\n```\n\nThis ensures that when ranks are equal, the lexicographically smaller node becomes the root. This is a deterministic tie-breaking rule.\n\nLet me finalize the implementation and format it as JSON.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the output format. The task says \"return selected edges plus total weight\". I should think about what fields to include. Let me include:\n- `mst_edges`: list of edges with their mutual reachability weights\n- `total_weight`: sum of all MST edge weights\n\nEach edge should have the canonicalized endpoint identifiers and the mutual reachability value.\n\nNow let me write the final Python code and encode it as JSON:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    # Validate required fields\n    if \"nodes\" not in case:\n        raise ValueError(\"Missing required field: nodes\")\n    if \"core_distance\" not in case:\n        raise ValueError(\"Missing required field: core_distance\")\n    if \"distances\" not in case:\n        raise ValueError(\"Missing required field: distances\")\n\n    nodes = list(case[\"nodes\"])\n    core_distance = dict(case[\"core_distance\"])\n    distances = list(case[\"distances\"])\n\n    n = len(nodes)\n    if n == 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"No nodes provided\")\n\n    # Validate all nodes have core distances\n    for node in nodes:\n        if node not in core_distance:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Missing core distance for node: {node}\")\n\n    # Compute mutual reachability edges\n    mr_edges = []\n    for edge in distances:\n        if len(edge) != 3:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Invalid edge format: {edge}\")\n        u, v, dist = edge[0], edge[1], float(edge[2])\n\n        if u not in core_distance:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Node {u} in distances not in core_distance\")\n        if v not in core_distance:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Node {v} in distances not in core_distance\")\n\n        mr = max(core_distance[u], core_distance[v], dist)\n\n        # Canonicalize: sort endpoints lexicographically\n        eu, ev = (u, v) if u \u003c= v else (v, u)\n\n        mr_edges.append((mr, eu, ev))\n\n    # Sort by mutual reachability, then by first endpoint, then second endpoint\n    mr_edges.sort(key=lambda e: (e[0], e[1], e[2]))\n\n    # Kruskal's algorithm with deterministic union-find\n    parent = {node: node for node in nodes}\n    rank = {node: 0 for node in nodes}\n\n    def find(x):\n        root = x\n        while parent[root] != root:\n            root = parent[root]\n        # Path compression\n        while parent[x] != root:\n            parent[x], x = root, parent[x]\n        return root\n\n    def union(x, y):\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\n        if rx == ry:\n            return False\n        # Union by rank with deterministic tie-break on node id\n        if rank[rx] \u003c rank[ry]:\n            rx, ry = ry, rx\n        elif rank[rx] == rank[ry] and rx \u003e ry:\n            rx, ry = ry, rx\n        parent[ry] = rx\n        if rank[rx] == rank[ry]:\n            rank[rx] += 1\n        return True\n\n    selected_edges = []\n    total_weight = 0.0\n\n    for mr, u, v in mr_edges:\n        if union(u, v):\n            selected_edges.append({\n                \"u\": u,\n                \"v\": v,\n                \"mutual_reachability\": mr\n            })\n            total_weight += mr\n            if len(selected_edges) == n - 1:\n                break\n\n    if len(selected_edges) != n - 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input graph is disconnected; cannot form a spanning tree\")\n\n    return {\n        \"mst_edges\": selected_edges,\n        \"total_weight\": total_weight\n    }\n```\n\nNow I need to format this as a JSON object. Let me encode the Python source as a JSON string with proper escaping.\n\nThe JSON response format should be:\n```json\n{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    ...\"}\n```\n\nLet me carefully construct this. I need to escape all newlines as \\n, all backslashes as \\\\, and all quotes as \\\".\n\nLet me write the code out cleanly first:\n\n```\ndef solve(case):\n    if \"nodes\" not in case:\n        raise ValueError(\"Missing required field: nodes\")\n    if \"core_distance\" not in case:\n        raise ValueError(\"Missing required field: core_distance\")\n    if \"distances\" not in case:\n        raise ValueError(\"Missing required field: distances\")\n\n    nodes = list(case[\"nodes\"])\n    core_distance = dict(case[\"core_distance\"])\n    distances = list(case[\"distances\"])\n\n    n = len(nodes)\n    if n == 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"No nodes provided\")\n\n    for node in nodes:\n        if node not in core_distance:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Missing core distance for node: {node}\")\n\n    mr_edges = []\n    for edge in distances:\n        if len(edge) != 3:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Invalid edge format: {edge}\")\n        u, v, dist = edge[0], edge[1], float(edge[2])\n        if u not in core_distance:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Node {u} not in core_distance\")\n        if v not in core_distance:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Node {v} not in core_distance\")\n        mr = max(core_distance[u], core_distance[v], dist)\n        eu, ev = (u, v) if u \u003c= v else (v, u)\n        mr_edges.append((mr, eu, ev))\n\n    mr_edges.sort(key=lambda e: (e[0], e[1], e[2]))\n\n    parent = {node: node for node in nodes}\n    rank = {node: 0 for node in nodes}\n\n    def find(x):\n        root = x\n        while parent[root] != root:\n            root = parent[root]\n        while parent[x] != root:\n            parent[x], x = root, parent[x]\n        return root\n\n    def union(x, y):\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\n        if rx == ry:\n            return False\n        if rank[rx] \u003c rank[ry]:\n            rx, ry = ry, rx\n        elif rank[rx] == rank[ry] and rx \u003e ry:\n            rx, ry = ry, rx\n        parent[ry] = rx\n        if rank[rx] == rank[ry]:\n            rank[rx] += 1\n        return True\n\n    selected_edges = []\n    total_weight = 0.0\n\n    for mr, u, v in mr_edges:\n        if union(u, v):\n            selected_edges.append({\"u\": u, \"v\": v, \"mutual_reachability\": mr})\n            total_weight += mr\n            if len(selected_edges) == n - 1:\n                break\n\n    if len(selected_edges) != n - 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input graph is disconnected; cannot form a spanning tree\")\n\n    return {\"mst_edges\": selected_edges, \"total_weight\": total_weight}\n```\n\nNow let me encode this properly. I'll produce the JSON response directly.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    if \\\"nodes\\\" not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Missing required field: nodes\\\")\\n    if \\\"core_distance\\\" not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Missing required field: core_distance\\\")\\n    if \\\"distances\\\" not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Missing required field: distances\\\")\\n\\n    nodes = list(case[\\\"nodes\\\"])\\n    core_distance = dict(case[\\\"core_distance\\\"])\\n    distances = list(case[\\\"distances\\\"])\\n\\n    n = len(nodes)\\n    if n == 0:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"No nodes provided\\\")\\n\\n    for node in nodes:\\n        if node not in core_distance:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Missing core distance for node: {node}\\\")\\n\\n    mr_edges = []\\n    for edge in distances:\\n        if len(edge) != 3:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Invalid edge format: {edge}\\\")\\n        u, v, dist = edge[0], edge[1], float(edge[2])\\n        if u not in core_distance:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Node {u} not found in core_distance\\\")\\n        if v not in core_distance:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Node {v} not found in core_distance\\\")\\n        mr = max(core_distance[u], core_distance[v], dist)\\n        eu, ev = (u, v) if u \u003c= v else (v, u)\\n        mr_edges.append((mr, eu, ev))\\n\\n    mr_edges.sort(key=lambda e: (e[0], e[1], e[2]))\\n\\n    parent = {node: node for node in nodes}\\n    rank = {node: 0 for node in nodes}\\n\\n    def find(x):\\n        root = x\\n        while parent[root] != root:\\n            root = parent[root]\\n        while parent[x] != root:\\n            parent[x], x = root, parent[x]\\n        return root\\n\\n    def union(x, y):\\n        rx, ry = find(x), find(y)\\n        if rx == ry:\\n            return False\\n        if rank[rx] \u003c rank[ry]:\\n            rx, ry = ry, rx\\n        elif rank[rx] == rank[ry] and rx \u003e ry:\\n            rx, ry = ry, rx\\n        parent[ry] = rx\\n        if rank[rx] == rank[ry]:\\n            rank[rx] += 1\\n        return True\\n\\n    selected_edges = []\\n    total_weight = 0.0\\n\\n    for mr, u, v in mr_edges:\\n        if union(u, v):\\n            selected_edges.append({\\\"u\\\": u, \\\"v\\\": v, \\\"mutual_reachability\\\": mr})\\n            total_weight += mr\\n            if len(selected_edges) == n - 1:\\n                break\\n\\n    if len(selected_edges) != n - 1:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Input graph is disconnected; cannot form a spanning tree\\\")\\n\\n    return {\\\"mst_edges\\\": selected_edges, \\\"total_weight\\\": total_weight}\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01BSwSg6qcOZ87tWHcF0aHBj","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2005},"cache_creation_input_tokens":2005,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":53,"output_tokens":3908,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3131},"service_tier":"standard"}}